- `action(n1, "start")`: Hallucinates an initial step; the description states the process begins directly with "HelloWorld.HelloWorld". (SMC1)
- `action(n3, "End")`: Misrepresents the process conclusion as an executable step instead of flowing directly to `end(e1)` after `action(n2, ...)`, contradicting "and then the process comes to an end". (SMC1, SMC2)
- `precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n1, n2), precedence(n2, n3), precedence(n3, e1)`: Chains the unmentioned actions into the control flow, breaking the exact chronological progression from "HelloWorld.HelloWorld" straight to termination required by the source. (SMC3, SMC5)